  o Minor features (onion service, introduction circuits):
    - Add a new per-service torrc option,
      HiddenServiceIntroCircuitRotation, which periodically rebuilds the
      internal circuit a service uses to reach each of its introduction
      points while keeping the same introduction point relay and the same
      introduction authentication key. The published descriptor is
      unchanged; only the guard, vanguard and middle hops rotate. The
      replacement circuit is built and established before the old one is
      dropped (make before break), so introductions are never
      interrupted. Disabled by default.
